Here is the PlantUML code for the class diagram based on the provided requirements:
@startuml
class Airline {
  - name : String
}

class Airport {
  - code : String
  - city : String
}

class Details {
  - operatingCost : Float
}

class Airline_Airport_Relation {
  - airline : Airline
  - airport : Airport
  - details : Details
}

Airline --* Airline_Airport_Relation
Airport --* Airline_Airport_Relation
Details --* Airline_Airport_Relation

@enduml
This PlantUML code defines the classes and relationships as described in the requirements. The `--*` symbol indicates a one-to-many relationship between an airline and its airport relations, an airport and its airline relations, and a details object associated with each relation.

Note that I've used the following notation:

* `- name : String` means that the class has a property named "name" of type String.
* `--*` means a one-to-many relationship between two classes.